<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78246" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρα-κόπτω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strike falsely, counterfeit</i>, prop. of money,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.78
			</span></i> : generally, <i>falsify</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίβδηλα καὶ νόθα καὶ παρακεκομμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ind.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			 ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόκιμα</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκίβδηλα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Herm.</u>
				68
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδράρια μοχθηρά,
			παρακεκομμένα</span> knavish manikins, <i>base coin</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				517
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>cheat</i> or <i>swindle out of</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἵων ἀγαθῶν παρεκόπτου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					807
				</span></i>
			; simply, <i>cheat</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				859
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be cheated</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρεκόπην διχοινίκῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					640
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>strike</i> the mind <i>awry, drive mad, derange</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. φρένας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					238
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακεκομμένος τὸν νοῦν</span>
				Sch.rec.<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				581
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>
			s.v.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> intr., <i>to be
			deranged</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ νοῦ παρακόπτοντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aff.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακόψαι τῇ διανοίᾴ</span>
			<i>go mad</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				832b17
			</span></i> : abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακόψας</span>
			<i>in a fit of madness</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				4.44
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.50
			</span></i> : so in pres., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακόπτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.963e
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				1123f
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κόψας</span>
			<i>wrongheadedly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				p.10
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>cut in pieces</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλη -κεκομμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					10.15.5
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>cut pieces off</i> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς
				πυέλου</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.29.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>cut across</i> a neck of land, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικαρσίᾳ τάφρῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					4.1.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>